**Lemma 5.3 (strict negative slope of the other positive-report ray).**
Throughout $0\leq a\leq a_\dagger$, one has $v_-<0<v_+$.

Proof. Let $r=\sqrt\alpha$, $\xi=2\beta a/D_a$,
$b=U_a/D_a=-1+\xi$ and $c=V_a/D_a>0$. Direct substitution gives

$$
\frac W{D_a^2}=
 (b/2-\xi k,\ 1/2+\alpha\xi kb,\ \beta\xi kc),
\quad
\frac{W_0+W_1/r}{D_a^2}
 =\frac{1/r-1}{2}+\xi[1/2-k(1+r-r\xi)].
\tag{TA.35}
$$

The supplied $.12227<\beta<.12230$ gives $.9368<r<.9370$
by squaring. Also $\xi'=2\beta(\alpha-a^2)/D_a^2>0$.
For $a\leq.28$, $\xi<.1475$ follows from
$2(.12230)(.28)<.1475[.87770(.44)+.28^2]$.
For $.28\leq a\leq a_\dagger<.2952$, $\xi<.1617$ follows from
$2(.12230)(.2952)<.1617[.87770(1-2(.2952))+.2952^2]$.
RC supplies $k<.4$ throughout and $k<.395$ on the latter interval.
Since $(1/r-1)/2>.0336$, TA.35 is bounded strictly below by

$$
\begin{cases}
.0336-.2748\xi+.37472\xi^2,&0\leq\xi\leq.1475,\\
.0336-.265115\xi+.370036\xi^2,&0\leq\xi\leq.1617,
\end{cases}
\tag{TA.36}
$$

on the respective $a$ intervals. The two quadratics decrease on the
indicated ranges. Their endpoint values are respectively
$.001219502>.0012$ and $.00040619508804>.0004$.
Thus $W_1>r(-W_0)>0$. Eliminating $u$ from the plane equation and
$\alpha u^2+\beta v^2=1$ yields a quadratic in $v$ with leading
coefficient $\alpha W_2^2+\beta W_1^2>0$ and constant coefficient
$\alpha W_0^2-W_1^2<0$. Its two roots have opposite signs; the
ordered formula TA.32 gives exactly $v_-<0<v_+$. Every comparison
above is an exact rational inequality on the supplied domains.
$\square$

